BEGIN_HYPERDESC
<h1>Impacts under high time acceleration</h1>
Delta-gliders hit the Moon under time acceleration, where a step moves a
vessel kilometres over the ground: one falling from 1,000 km at 1,000x,
one on an orbit whose periapsis is below the ground at 10,000x (the
stabilised propagator). Each must be set down on the terrain and landed,
in normal time, without its state going bad; a third, in a high orbit,
must keep flying.
END_HYPERDESC

BEGIN_ENVIRONMENT
  System Sol
  Date MJD 51982.6685767396
  Script Tests/ImpactWarpTest
END_ENVIRONMENT

BEGIN_FOCUS
  Ship HIGH
END_FOCUS

BEGIN_CAMERA
  TARGET HIGH
  MODE Extern
  POS 4 0 -20
  TRACKMODE TargetRelative
  FOV 50.00
END_CAMERA

BEGIN_SHIPS
FALL:DeltaGlider
  STATUS Orbiting Moon
  ELEMENTS 1.0e7 0.00000 0.0 0.0 0.0 0.0 51982.6685767396
  AROT 0 0 0
END
DIVE:DeltaGlider
  STATUS Orbiting Moon
  ELEMENTS 2.5e6 0.40000 30.0 0.0 0.0 180.0 51982.6685767396
  AROT 0 0 0
END
HIGH:DeltaGlider
  STATUS Orbiting Moon
  ELEMENTS 3.0e6 0.00000 60.0 0.0 0.0 90.0 51982.6685767396
  AROT 0 0 0
END
END_SHIPS
